Relational operator:
Result of relational operator is either true or false.
True or false is belongs to boolean data type.
Old version of C language doesnot have a support for boolean datetype .Hense , compiler will take true as 1, false as 0.
In new version of C language boolean support is there.
< > <= >= == !=
eg:
#include <stdio.h>
void  main() {
    int a,b;
    a=10,b=29;
   printf("%d\n",a>b);   
     printf("%d\n",a<b); 
       printf("%d\n",a>=b); 
         printf("%d\n",a<=b); 
           printf("%d\n",a==b); 
             printf("%d\n",a!=b); 
             
}
